# gem5 observation-only patch — W5X3-OBS-0222 (M07-C02 squash-discard terminal)

Round 0222 · `gem5-fi-mmu-when5x3` · 2026-11-19
New build hash: `ce80a9c983b31f77c9b4a6626012505fd3484d5c00df5b9399a9d6975ab2b73d`

Purpose: prove, at runtime, the COMPLETE fault->terminal lifecycle of the
M07-C02-T01/T02 squashed loads.  Previously the chain was inferred to stop at
`lsu_request` (no downstream events = "request pending at ROI end").  This
patch adds pure-observation events in the O3 LSQ translation-completion path
so the actual discard branch is visible in the trace.

Observation-only: nothing changes translation/dispatch behavior.  The 8
matching Controls reproduce frozen N (M07-C02 N=6) and the guest SIGSEGV
pattern is byte-identical to the historical runs.

## New event kinds (fault_id joins the whole chain; parent_event_id chains them)

  translation_response_received
  squash_translation_decision     (decision=continue_normal|discard_due_to_prior_squash)
  squash_translation_invoked      (released=1 -> self-destruct)
  translation_request_discarded   (terminal_reason=prior_squash_before_translation_completion)
  cache_dispatch_decision         (dispatch_decision=cache_dispatch_blocked_by_squash)

