## Change 2 — src/cpu/o3/CHAOSPropagation/CHAOSPropagation.cc

Add CHAOSPropagation::mmuNoteLsqTranslationFinish (after mmuNoteLsuRequest).
It resolves tid via mmuTxnForSeqVa(seq,va)/mmuTxnForSeq(seq), then emits the
parent-chained event sequence.  Identity fields: fault_id (ftid),
translation_id, unique_request_id, dyn_inst_seq, request_id, va, pc, asid,
fault_status, lq_idx, pa; plus decision/released/squash_cause/
terminal_reason/cleanup_completed/dispatch_decision/rejection_reason.

  - translation_response_received  parent = txn.last_event (the open lsu_request)
  - squash_translation_decision    decision = continue_normal | discard_due_to_prior_squash
  - [if prior_squash]
      squash_translation_invoked   released = isReleased()
      translation_request_discarded terminal_reason = prior_squash_before_translation_completion
      cache_dispatch_decision      dispatch_decision = cache_dispatch_blocked_by_squash

## Change 3 — src/cpu/o3/lsq.cc  (LSQ::SingleDataRequest::finish)

@@ after `numTranslatedFragments = 1;`, before the isSquashed() branch @@
+    /* [W5X3-OBS-0222] Observe the translation-response handoff and the
+     * squash-discard decision so the fault->LSU->squash-terminal chain is
+     * proven at runtime (not inferred from the absence of a cache_request).
+     * Pure observation; never changes translation/dispatch behaviour. */
+    if (_inst && _inst->cpu && _inst->cpu->chaosPropagation) {
+        const bool prior_squash = _inst->isSquashed();
+        const bool released = isReleased();
+        const char *fs = (fault == NoFault) ? "NoFault"
+                          : (fault ? fault->name() : "NoFault");
+        const Addr pa = request->hasPaddr() ? request->getPaddr() : 0;
+        _inst->cpu->chaosPropagation->mmuNoteLsqTranslationFinish(
+            request, _inst.get(), fs, pa, prior_squash, released);
+    }

No other change.  The `if (_inst->isSquashed()) { squashTranslation(); }`
branch and the normal `setState(State::Request)` branch are unchanged.

